## Goal
Close a gap found in cross-review of PR #13 (DEV-46): the guard in the build script refuses a build directory inside `~/Applications`, but it was bypassed when `~/Applications` did not yet exist. Add a regression test for it in `scripts/test-install.sh`.

## Problems
- The guard resolves `~/Applications` after `mkdir -p "$OUT"`, so when the directory was absent at the start, the build could land inside its own install destination. Codex review flagged this.
- Manual reproduction with a fresh temporary HOME and a build dir under `Applications/sub` showed the build script already refuses it (exit 1). However, the `Applications` directory was left behind in the temp HOME as a side effect.

## Decision
Extend `scripts/test-install.sh` with a case using a fresh HOME that has no `Applications` directory. It runs `scripts/build-app.sh` with `PORTERO_BUILD_DIR` set to `Applications/sub` and expects a refusal (failure). This pins the behaviour so the guard cannot regress, and keeps the test isolated in a temporary directory.

